[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged **412 unique reports** (the export lists 427 rows because its
pages overlap; one id is one report). The merge was made on the subject line
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by cause, the reports hold
three different problems.

<Callout>
One fix will not close this ticket. Fixing the parser leaves 33 reports unexplained.
</Callout>

## What is in it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| # | Problem | Reports | Fix belongs to |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `parser` reads every date month first; day-first tenants get flipped dates | 379 | shared date parser |
| 2 | `hint`: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people at day-first tenants (`alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, `pale.harbour`) type month first | 33 | booking-v3 form hint |
| 3 | One-day shift: a date lands a day off, not a month flip (desk notes `oneDayMove`: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) | 5 | timezone / day boundary, to investigate |

379 + 33 = 412, the desk view. It counts the five one-day reports under `parser`, because it
places reports by tenant. Their text does not fit a month/day swap, so they also get their own ticket (5, already inside the 379).

## Why the first merge hid this

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant: where they
are and which booking form they run. Matching on subject cannot see either.

## Next

- One ticket per problem, each with its report count.
- Re-read the five one-day reports before closing the third ticket.

